  HOW TO READ -- two traps, both live in this table:
   1. macroAP/macroF1 are per-column cosine metrics: EXACTLY invariant in K
      by construction. Their flatness is arithmetic, not evidence.
   2. top3F1 can RISE with K without accuracy improving: distractors take
      slots in the top-3, so fewer REAL columns are predicted per row
      (see nreal/row) and precision goes up for free. Not a scaling win.
  The uncontaminated verdict is steal@1 (a distractor beating every real
  policy on a genuinely harmful row) and meanRank read against chance.
